        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "There's ONE failure here right now.\r\n\r\ncheckhealth [now sources help.lua too](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40723/changes#diff-56911793c36166f3805fdeb7eea9a6d08bfb7099f17eb5e1020438fbda19bbca). **This applies help-like ts syntax highlighting to checkhealth files, in addition to checkhealth syntax.**\r\n\r\nAFAIK we source help.vim because the checkhealth buffer is \"help-like.\" But it's not *super* help-like, since enabling help.lua brings a bunch of unwanted stuff.\r\n\r\ndoing something like stopping treesitter in a new checkhealth.lua doesn't smell right. any ideas?",
