        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Since checkhealth is a purely Neovim concept, we should just port that one to Lua and source the (single) right one we want. Although honestly, I don't see why we want to source either -- none of the health ftplugin settings seem relevant to checkhealth buffers since they're not editable...\r\n\r\n(Personally, I have pushed very strongly to keep Neovim runtime files in Lua for the purpose of clear separation of concerns, even at the cost of Lua->Vimscript indirection. I have been fairly alone in that...)",
